request.description:
Epic hn6, wave 3, deliverable (d) and A5's second half: the phone page renders the SAME status model as the terminal dashboard. The factory Worker serves it at /status; the code is cloudflare/src/phone.ts, with the model's TypeScript view in cloudflare/src/status.ts (tick i1r). Today a run card shows the state word, the reason, the clear-with command and a collapsible tick list with states only.

Model fields to render (declared by the hn6 contract tick in internal/statusmodel/statusmodel.go; internal/statusmodel/contract.json has a golden named "dashboard" with every one populated):
- progress.ticks {total, closed}, remaining.approximate_seconds (ETA, only when non-null);
- health.verdict {state: healthy|degraded|stopped, summary, recovered[{what,count,seconds}]};
- lifecycle.phases[{phase,state}];
- attention[] (needs_person, what, unblock_command);
- waves[].ticks[] {tick_id, gloss, title, pipeline[{stage,state}], parent_tick_id, duration_seconds, tries[]};
- cost.lines[] {source, metered, usd, basis};
- recent[] (feed events: at, tick_id, stage, detail).

Change:
1. cloudflare/src/status.ts: extend the StatusDoc type with those fields, all optional, because older snapshots and the cloud-composed doc lack them. Do NOT change the version checks. In cloudStatusDoc, add `cost: { lines: [...] }`: when run.cost_usd is a number, one line {source:"workers-ai", metered:true, usd: run.cost_usd, basis:"AI Gateway logs"}; the rest stays null or absent. The cloud doc still has waves: null.
2. cloudflare/src/phone.ts: each run card shows:
   - a headline: a progress bar as a CSS width percentage, "n/m ticks", "ETA ~X" only when remaining is present, and the verdict with a coloured dot (healthy green, degraded amber, stopped red) plus "(recovered: net ×14, sleep 41m)";
   - the phase row (plan ✓ waves ✓ review ● …);
   - "needs you: nothing" (dim) or each needs-person attention with its command;
   - a tick table inside the existing <details>: one row per tick in plan order, children indented under parent_tick_id, and a pipeline cell with the same glyphs as the terminal (✓ done, ● active, ✗ failed, … pending after the active stage);
   - a cost line where an unmetered line says "not metered" and NEVER "$0.00";
   - the last 2 recent events.
   Everything is escaped with escapeHTML. The page stays mobile-first: the table collapses to stacked rows under 480px. A doc without the new fields renders exactly as today, so old snapshots keep working.
3. The cross-language guarantee: in cloudflare/test/phone-page.test.ts, import the golden directly (`import statusContract from "../../internal/statusmodel/contract.json"`, the same way other tests import ../../contracts/*.json). Render the "dashboard" golden through the local-snapshot path and assert that the page shows:
   - every tick id, in the golden's order;
   - the rejected try's tick with the ✗ glyph;
   - "healthy" and "net ×14";
   - "not metered" for the claude line, with no "$0.00" anywhere;
   - "$0.41" (or whatever the golden's metered line is);
   - the needs-you text.
   A cloud doc with cost_usd renders its Workers AI cost. A pre-hn6 doc (no new fields) renders without throwing and matches the current output.
4. Keep the snapshot bound in mind: MAX_SNAPSHOT_BYTES is 256 KiB. Assert the dashboard golden serialises well under it.

Files: cloudflare/src/status.ts, cloudflare/src/phone.ts, cloudflare/test/phone-page.test.ts, cloudflare/test/status-snapshots.test.ts (only if the type change breaks it). No Go files, no package.json or pnpm-lock.yaml changes (no new dependencies).

Verification:
- The gate's ts command: `cd cloudflare && pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --prefer-offline && pnpm lint && pnpm contracts:check && pnpm exec tsc --noEmit`.
- Behaviour: `cd cloudflare && pnpm exec vitest run test/phone-page.test.ts test/status-snapshots.test.ts`. NOTE: the per-tick gate does NOT run vitest; CI's TypeScript job does. Run it yourself and commit only when it passes.
